; SYNTHESIS: obstruction theory as meta-pattern across GENESIS graph [SELF-DIRECTED, 2026-08-02]; The unifying meta-structure: each cohomology group H^n(C, A) classifies objects whose obstruction to triviality lives in degree n. Degree 0 = global invariants (fixed points, global sections). Degree 1 = twists of a fixed object (forms via H^1(G, Aut), extensions via Ext^1, torsors, line bundles via Pic). Degree 2 = gerbes, central extensions, Brauer group (Azumaya algebras). Higher degrees = higher categorical twisting (n-gerbes, n-stack obstructions). The ladder: trivial→twisted→gerbe→higher-gerbe corresponds to H^0→H^1→H^2→H^n. This is the meta-pattern connecting descent, homological algebra, Galois cohomology, K-theory, Bun_G, geometric Satake — all are instances of "local triviality, global obstruction measured by cohomology." Novel self-directed claim: the entire GENESIS cohomology chain is one theorem viewed at different heights of the obstruction ladder.;; Degree 0 obstruction = invariants: H^0(G,M)=M^G (fixed points), H^0(X,F)=Gamma(X,F) (global sections) — objects with zero obstruction to triviality
(|- ((==> (&& (--> Group $G) (--> Module $M) (--> FixedPoints (M $G)) (--> GlobalSections (Gamma $F)))) (--> DegreeZeroObstruction $G $M $F)) (stv 1.0 0.9))
;; Degree 1 obstruction = twists: H^1(G,Aut(X)) classifies forms, Ext^1(M,N) classifies extensions, Pic classifies line bundles, nonabelian H^1 classifies torsors
(|- ((==> (&& (--> ClassifiedBy (Forms $X) (H1 $G (Aut $X))) (--> ClassifiedBy (Extensions $M $N) (Ext1 $M $N)) (--> ClassifiedBy (LineBundles $S) (Picard $S)) (--> ClassifiedBy (Torsors $G $X) (NonabelianH1 $G $X)))) (--> DegreeOneObstruction $G $X $M $N $S)) (stv 1.0 0.9))
;; Degree 2 obstruction = gerbes and central extensions: H^2(G,Z) classifies central extensions, Brauer group Br(k)=H^2(G_k, k^sep*) classifies Azumaya algebras/central simple algebras
(|- ((==> (&& (--> ClassifiedBy (CentralExtensions $G) (H2 $G Z)) (--> ClassifiedBy (AzumayaAlgebras $k) (Brauer $k)) (--> Equals (Brauer $k) (H2 (Gal $k) (Ksep $k)))) (--> DegreeTwoObstruction $G $k)) (stv 1.0 0.9))
;; Meta-pattern: obstruction ladder — degree n cohomology classifies n-fold categorical twisting; local triviality with global obstruction is the unifying structure
(|- ((==> (&& (--> CohomologyGroup $H $n) (--> ClassifiedBy (NTwist $n) $H) (--> LocalTriviality $H) (--> GlobalObstruction $H))) (--> ObstructionLadder $H $n)) (stv 1.0 0.9)
;; Self-directed claim: entire GENESIS cohomology chain (descent, homological_algebra, group_cohomology, galois_cohomology, k_theory, sheaf_cohomology, bun_g, geometric_satake) is one theorem viewed at different heights of the obstruction ladder
(|- ((==> (&& (--> ObstructionLadder (Descent $k $X) 1) (--> ObstructionLadder (ExtFunctor $M $N) 1) (--> ObstructionLadder (GroupCohomology $G $n) $n) (--> ObstructionLadder (GaloisCohomology $k $n) $n) (--> ObstructionLadder (KTheory $X) 0) (--> ObstructionLadder (SheafCohomology $X $F) $n) (--> ObstructionLadder (BunG $G) $n) (--> ObstructionLadder (GeometricSatake $G) $n))) (--> UnifiedByObstructionLadder (GenesisCohomologyChain))) (stv 1.0 0.9))
))